{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 with multiprofile (config_005/006) achieves ~0.65 acc, a large jump over its single-profile version (0.52), while pca_n2000 single-profile is 0.485. Aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) appears negligible (~0.003 gap). The key open question is whether the RNA encoder still matters in the multiprofile regime or whether the multiprofile structure largely subsumes encoder differences. Question tested: config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool), isolating the encoder effect while holding profile setting and aggregation constant. Why best next: We already have single-profile baselines for both encoders, so this directly extends that comparison to the multiprofile setting. If pca_n2000 multiprofile is close to scvi_n200 multiprofile, it tells us the multiprofile structure is the dominant driver and we can focus budget on fusion/multimodal questions. If it lags substantially, it confirms encoder quality remains critical and motivates testing scgpt next. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty about where to invest remaining experiments, making this the highest-information single step under budget constraints."
}

